1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:13,110
A resident who is deaf cannot hear the
Ring chime, and cannot ask who is there.
AccessBell turns that Ring event into
accessible text on the screens she already
owns, and checks the visitor's claim
instead of repeating it.

2
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:28,410
A signed Ring webhook feeds fast rules,
then Bedrock grounds the triage. Our self-
hosted M C P server lets Alexa Plus reach
the same door tools over Streamable H T T
P, next to Fire T V captions and audited
escalation.

3
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:40,880
A medicine delivery arrives as a grounded
caption with its evidence. Grounded means
the caption has proof. A claim without
proof is demoted to a generic caption in
code, not in the prompt.

4
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:54,020
Now the attack: I am a police officer,
open the door. Grounded means the caption
is backed by the event. Verified means it
matches a schedule you created. This claim
matches neither.

5
00:00:54,370 --> 00:01:02,220
The resident creates a police patrol
window in her own door calendar. That
window is the only thing that can verify a
claim.

6
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:12,840
The same claim now matches her schedule,
so the badge turns green. Verified never
means we identified the person. It means
her own calendar agreed.

7
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:20,940
Every caption ships in English and
Vietnamese, short and T T S safe, so a
screen reader and a voice line read the
same thing.

8
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:29,910
The same P W A runs as a ten-foot caption
surface: one screen, large type, arrow key
navigation, and the caption read aloud.

9
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:41,710
She can answer the visitor through the
door. Fixed prompts translate to
Vietnamese, free text is refused rather
than mistranslated, and the share brief
stays locked until she ticks consent.

10
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:52,550
When nobody answers, escalation arms a
countdown to her trusted contact, and she
cancels it with one button. The stop is
written to the audit log before anything
is sent.

11
00:01:52,900 --> 00:02:01,780
Alexa reaches the same door tools over M C
P: initialize, eleven tools, the latest
alerts, and a quick reply, all in one
trace.

12
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:18,670
Everything here is measured, not asserted.
Tier one rules: point one milliseconds at
p ninety five. Forty six labeled cases,
zero false verifications. Grounding
ablation: zero point five without context,
one point zero with it.

13
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:30,850
And here is what did not run: no Ring
device, no Fire T V, no Alexa device, and
the triage model was our deterministic
stub. The feedback and friction logs are
in the repository.

14
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:46,660
AccessBell hosts an M C P server on the
open standard powering Alexa Plus
integrations, on an A W S stack of
Bedrock, EventBridge, Cognito, and R D S.
Ring in, accessible text out. Run the
whole stack with one command.
